  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Find the fix in the noise.",
    "overview": "The homepage opens with a gateway 503 alert and follows it from the closest text match to a recorded relationship and a suggested check. In the final chapter, the repository mirror replay shows how the results change when a responder saves a fix. The full-bleed field draws or retracts each path when the comparison changes.\n\nThe workspace carries that vocabulary into a focused evidence pane. Warm charcoal surfaces set off a connected precedent, source identifiers, and relationship actions.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-black surfaces with warm white type and orange actions.",
      "Bricolage Grotesque for reading and IBM Plex Mono for labels and identifiers.",
      "Streamline Pixel Mono Free icons with functional text.",
      "A scroll-driven constellation, open evidence comparisons, and a focused console evidence pane."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Relationship Rule",
        "body": "Pair the orange path with a relationship label, source identifiers, and a caption or explanation.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** pair orange relationship paths with labels and source identifiers.",
      "**Do** keep Streamline Pixel icons alongside action text where space allows.",
      "**Do** keep the vector baseline reachable from the evidence pane at all widths.",
      "**Do** distinguish illustrative layout from the recorded relationship."
    ],
